# The Bible sources are byte-sensitive and must round-trip through git
# unchanged.
#
# Three of the four (ELB, KJV, S51) are CRLF as published, and git's default
# `text=auto` would normalise them to LF on the next checkout — which changes
# the bytes, and these bytes are load-bearing twice over: `bible:build` records
# a `sha256` per pack, and `bible:verify` asserts the JS parser agrees with the
# PHP parser on golden fixtures generated from the file the server actually
# serves. A clone whose XML had been silently re-lined would fail that
# comparison for a reason nobody would look for.
#
# `binary` is `-text -diff`: never convert, and don't try to diff a 5 MB
# single-line XML either.
public/bibles/*.xml binary

# Generated packs are gzip and JSON blobs, hashed the same way.
public/bible-packs/**/*.json binary
public/bible-packs/**/*.gz   binary
